 "_about": "What each consumer does with a declared fact, as data (LIBRARY_DESIGN.md 4.4; ROADMAP M3.1). One row per consumer and fact field. 'honours' true: the consumer applies the declared value; false: it runs without it. 'evidence' says how that is known: measured (a probe: runs with the fact bound and removed differ, and two control runs agree), code (read in the installed source), documented (the engine's documentation). A probe that shows a difference only proves that some path reads the fact; where a code reading found a path that drops it, the row says false and the note keeps the measurement. Consumers are named engine.role.name, and engine.role is a group of consumers that can stand in for one another; 'prefer' lists, per group, the consumers a resolution may route to, in order. transformers.paged_attention is its own group: continuous batching can only switch to another paged kernel, and none is measured to honour softcap. Only rows with measured evidence count for routing. Measured rows: Gemma 2 2B (gemma-2-2b-it) on an RTX 4070 Ti (sm_89).",
